+        "team": "3 Designers, 8 Engineers, 2 Product Managers",
+        "platform": ["iOS", "Android"],
+        "tools": ["Figma", "React Native", "TypeScript", "Reanimated", "Firebase"],
+        "industry": "FinTech"
+      },
+      "sections": {
+        "problem": "A legacy investment platform with a desktop-first mentality was losing younger users who expected a mobile-native experience. The existing app had a 3.2-star rating, 4.8s load times, and a 31% drop-off rate during the account opening flow. Users found it difficult to track portfolio performance, execute trades, and understand risk exposure on small screens.\n\nThe core challenge was translating dense financial data and complex trading workflows into a mobile experience that felt fast, trustworthy, and intuitive - without dumbing down the functionality that professional users relied on.",
+        "research": {
+          "methods": [
+            "Diary study with 18 users across 2 weeks tracking mobile banking habits",
